# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# API keys / secrets
.env
*.key
credentials.*

# Temp files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Claude Code scratch files (PR/issue body drafts)
.pr-body.md
.issue-comment.md

# Test-coverage artifacts (regenerable; coverage may be run from the repo root)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Claude Code runtime state. `settings.local.json` was tracked until 2026-09-14
# and is not any more: it is per-machine permission state, not project
# configuration. By the time it was removed every entry in it referenced a file
# that no longer existed (`cyber_threat_prompt.md`, `cyber_threat_skill.yaml`,
# `docs.md`, `schema_json.json`, `examples_outputs.json`) and it carried a
# `git push origin main` grant — one contributor's local trust decisions,
# committed for everyone and silently stale.
#
# Ignored by exact name rather than ignoring `.claude/` wholesale: project
# skills live at `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and must stay trackable.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.lock
# Claude Code agent worktrees (managed by the SDK, not project files)
.claude/worktrees/

# Python artifacts
# Root-level now that Python lives in two places (mcp/ and evals/); mcp/ has
# its own .gitignore predating this, which stays as the more specific rule.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Threat-intel runs. reports/ is a FROZEN eval corpus (see CLAUDE.md); a
# dispatched run writes here instead and is published to the run summary,
# so a helpful run leaves no permanent history.
report-output/

# Scenario-run output (#185). Local evidence for the run that produced it, not
# repository history: reports/ is a frozen corpus CI pins at 11, and committing
# these would recreate the growing fixture set that freeze exists to stop.
evals/runs/
